N2  - Summary Additive manufacturing (AM), commonly known as three-dimensional (3D) printing, has emerged as a revolutionary technology capable of fabricating parts with complex geometries in a layer-by-layer manner, thereby granting unprecedented design freedom. Powder?based AM is a major subset of the AM family, in which powders are used as the feedstock materials to fabricate parts. This chapter presents a brief introduction to metal powder?based AM, including the history and fundamentals of AM, representative AM categories, metal powder?based AM techniques, post-processing for metal AM parts, and powder properties and characterization methods.
