N2  - Summary The chapter focuses on the achievements of 5G networks to provide the first roadmap toward 6G and beyond networks in terms of requirements, use-case scenarios and service classes. It presents potential technologies that will be dominant through 2025?2030 in shaping the vision of 6G and beyond networks. The chapter provides various features and technologies as well as challenges and research directions in 6G and beyond networks. 5G networks are offering several advancements regarding the network softwarization and virtualization, new frequency bands, massive Multiple-Input Multiple-Output, massive Internet of Things, ultradensification etc. The chapter provides aspects of 6G innovations that leverage the network management, automation and orchestration, pervasive artificial intelligence, machine learning, and big data analytics, new protocol stack, and 3D network architectures. The academia and industry have started to establish the service requirements for the coming decade.
